---
// Case №01 MALTALINK (Phase 5 §5.3) — the vertical slice's exemplar case:
// full anatomy PROBLEM/CONSTRAINT flat on grid -> DECISION lifted card ->
// EVIDENCE blue plate -> RESULT green band -> LESSON bare pull-quote.
// Phase 6B register (motion prop): kicker/headline/hero settle at load;
// PROBLEM onward join via scroll-reveal. RESULT is the numeric outcome
// band, so it carries the one-per-page beat (data-register-beat).
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Rail from "../../components/Rail.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import TickRule from "../../components/TickRule.astro";
import Placeholder from "../../components/Placeholder.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";

// Phase 7 C1 meta table, verbatim.
const title = "MALTALINK 2025 — 100% registration completion · №01";
const description =
  "One flow instead of two systems: Ticket Tailor over Eventbrite, proven by live demo — 100% completion, 0 downtime, ~€1,000 saved.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} motion>
  <Rail>
    <div class="cell">
      <div class="clab">RECORD</div>
      <div class="cell-name">№01 MALTALINK</div>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <div class="clab">ROLE</div>
      <div class="cell-val">
        Web development — sole owner; worked closely with co-designer (PR
        Manager)
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cell-pair">
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="clab">SPAN</div>
        <div class="cell-val-mono">4-5 mo</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="clab">YEAR</div>
        <div class="cell-val-mono">2025</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Nav current="work" workSuffix="1/5" />
    <div class="rail-foot">
      <div class="clab">TOOLS</div>
      <div class="rail-chips" style="margin-top: 4px">
        <span class="stk">Ticket Tailor</span>
        <span class="stk">WordPress</span>
        <span class="stk">Astra</span>
      </div>
      <a
        href="https://conference2025.district109.org"
        class="rail-link"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">↗ conference2025.district109.org</a
      >
    </div>
  </Rail>

  <div class="mm col case">
    <span class="kicker" data-register
      >DECISION №01 — REGISTRATION PLATFORM</span
    >
    <h1 class="h1-case exemplar" data-register>
      One flow instead of two systems — every purchaser registered.
    </h1>
    <p class="case-lede-metrics">
      100% COMPLETION · ~€1,000 SAVED · 0 DOWNTIME · 4.55/5 SURVEY
    </p>

    <Placeholder
      slug="maltalink-hero"
      kind="WIDE / HERO — 16:7 DESKTOP · 16:9 MOBILE"
      style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 7"
      data-register="lg"
    />

    <div class="block" data-register>
      <span class="eb eb-neutral">PROBLEM</span>
      <p class="prose block-body">
        The 2024 conference ran on two disconnected systems — Eventbrite took
        payment while a separate Google Form collected registration details.
        Attendees dropped off between the two steps, the datasets never quite
        matched, and organizers spent evenings manually chasing people who had
        paid but never registered. The District IT Manager named this the single
        biggest pain point to fix for 2025.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="block" data-register>
      <span class="eb eb-neutral">CONSTRAINT</span>
      <p class="prose block-body">
        Phased deadlines across 4-5 months, with registration, finance, and
        volunteering teams each holding requirements. The IT Manager favored the
        fast path — tools already familiar and licensed — and time pressure made
        pragmatic shortcuts tempting throughout.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dcard dcard-static" data-register="lg">
      <span class="eb">DECISION</span>
      <p class="prose block-note">
        One stakeholder with real influence said further research wasn't worth
        doing. I ran a focused comparison anyway — respectfully — and brought a
        live demo instead of an argument. Side by side, Astra + Ticket Tailor
        won on flexibility, richer registration forms, centralized PDF/CSV
        export, automatic QR-code check-in, and far lower ongoing fees. The
        demo, not my opinion, moved the decision — and registration became a
        mandatory step inside checkout, collapsing two systems into one flow.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="evidence" data-register="lg">
      <span class="eb">EVIDENCE</span>
      <div class="evidence-figs">
        <Placeholder
          slug="maltalink-before-after"
          kind="PAIRED — STACKS ON MOBILE"
          style="height: 180px"
        />
        <Placeholder
          slug="maltalink-ticket-tailor"
          kind="WIDE"
          style="height: 180px"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="prose evidence-caption">
        Ticket Tailor cost €84 total for the conference vs ~13x that on
        Eventbrite for the same job — close to €1,000 kept. The before/after
        shows the fragmented two-system flow against the single checkout.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="result" data-register="lg" data-register-beat>
      <span class="rb">RESULT</span>
      <p class="result-metrics">
        100% COMPLETION · 0 DOWNTIME · 4.55/5 SURVEY · ~€1,000 SAVED
      </p>
      <p class="prose block-note">
        Every ticket purchaser completed registration — the mandatory checkout
        step made drop-off structurally impossible. Launched November 2025 and
        ran without downtime through the conference; the post-conference survey
        rated registration and website 4.55/5. Recognition followed: an official
        certificate of appreciation, a public LinkedIn recommendation citing
        ownership, vision, and a crash-free launch, and an invitation into the
        Website Manager role for 2026.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-register>
      <TickRule variant="light" style="max-width: 196px; margin-bottom: 8px" />
      <p class="lesson">
        <span class="lesson-label">LESSON — </span>Sometimes the person with
        influence will tell you research isn't worth doing. Run it anyway,
        respectfully, and let the side-by-side make the case. Compromise on the
        day-to-day; hold firm with evidence on the few calls that matter.
      </p>
    </div>

    <TickRule variant="light" />

    <Footer data-register>
      <a href="/work/foltirana" class="ftl" slot="left">← №05 FOLTIRANA</a>
      <a href="/work/mystore" class="ftl" slot="right">№02 MYSTORE →</a>
    </Footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Mock padding "28px 34px", gap "12px" x1.636 (Phase 7 scale factor) */
  .case {
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 46px var(--col-pad);
  }

  /* Mobile collapses to the uniform inset, same as Home: mock 10px and
     7px x1.44 -> --space-4 and --space-3 on the existing scale. */
  @media (width < 64rem) {
    .case {
      gap: var(--space-3);
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--col-pad);
    }
  }

  /* MALTALINK is a deliberate one-off: mock headline is 24px vs the
     22px-mock norm baked into the shared --fs-h1-case (see tokens.css) */
  .exemplar {
    font-size: 39px; /* 24px x1.636 */
  }

  /* DECISION/RESULT body text, mock margin-top "6px" x1.636 */
  .block-note {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  /* EVIDENCE caption, mock margin-top "8px" x1.636 */
  .evidence-caption {
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
</style>
